Dual/Symmetric Modeling

      Can I solve the opposite/complement/symmetric version more easily?

      Example
            Subarrays with Exactly K Distinct Integers

      How
            Instead of counting exactly K directly, compute atMost(K) - atMost(K-1)
            Complex exact counting → simpler complementary counting

      Fails when:
            Complement/opposite version is equally hard or loses important information.
            Example
                Problems where valid configurations cannot be derived cleanly from invalid ones.

Brain flips perspective, but transformed version does not actually simplify state or computation.

      
            
